# Mac mini only packages.
#
# Applied after the shared Brewfile by scripts/init.sh, which picks this file from
# scripts/host-profile.sh. The split is by machine, not by GUI vs CLI: the Mac mini is
# used interactively too, so anything that is not machine-specific stays in Brewfile.

# Local LLM runtime. The formula rather than an app bundle, so it can be kept running by
# a launchd job on a headless machine. The model directory moves with OLLAMA_MODELS once
# the external NVMe arrives, which is why nothing here hardcodes a path.
brew "ollama"

# Tailscale, as the formula rather than the GUI app the laptop gets. Its service stanza is
# require_root, so tailscaled runs as a root LaunchDaemon and is up before anyone logs in
# -- which is what recovering unattended after a power cut needs. Its state lives in
# /var/lib/tailscale and never touches the login keychain, so it stays inside the rule that
# LaunchDaemons hold no secrets.
brew "tailscale"

# DDC control for the two LG monitors, so their input is switched from this machine rather
# than from the joystick on the back of each one. It has to be this machine: the other two
# that use the monitors are a company MacBook, which cannot have software installed on it,
# and a personal one -- and the Mac mini is the one that is always on. The display_mode
# role places the scripts that drive it.
brew "m1ddc"

# Keeps macOS from dropping a display while its input is pointed at another machine. That
# is the one failure the display_mode role cannot recover from: a monitor macOS no longer
# sees takes no DDC command, so there is no way back to the Mac mini except the joystick.
cask "betterdisplay"

# The buttons the display modes are actually used from. The .app wrappers that
# build-apps.sh produces are assigned to them with the "System > Open" action, which is why
# no Stream Deck plugin is needed.
cask "elgato-stream-deck"
